  "id": "red-cliffs",
  "name": "Red Cliffs",
  "year": 208,
  "title": "The Fire at Red Cliffs",
  "place": "Chibi, on the Yangtze",
  "blurb": [
    "Cao Cao has brought eight hundred thousand men, or so his letters claim, down the Yangtze, and his northern soldiers, who cannot stand on a rolling deck, have had their ships chained bow to stern to make a floating road. Sun Quan's admiral Zhou Yu holds the southern bank with Liu Bei's company beside him.",
    "A fleet that cannot cast loose cannot flee. Fire is the answer, but all the early autumn the wind has blown from the north-west, straight back onto the south bank. Huang Gai has promised to bring fire ships alongside the moment it turns. Hold the shore, keep your hands cool, and be ready when it does."
  ],
